  "observations": [
    "All 55 checkbox glyphs and eight bilingual Yes/No pairs on final terms Part I pages 3–7 agree with the selected/deleted inventory. Unselected Option II fields are counted but their parent is excluded.",
    "TARGET appears in two different contexts: the floating-rate section is unchecked; the payment-system TARGET option is checked.",
    "The dated issuer call is Yes; the separate interest-date call is No. The make-whole and clean-up calls are Yes; the transaction-trigger and renminbi calls are No.",
    "The scheduled holder put is No, while the separate change-of-control holder right is Yes. The rating condition, definitions and exercise procedure on German base pages 119–120 remain material.",
    "The German clean-up clause on page 122 requires acquisition of at least 75% of original principal AND reduction in the global note. It covers the whole residual issue with 30–60 days notice, par and accrued interest.",
    "The Finance-only initial guarantee on German base pages 110–111 is excluded for the initial BASF SE issuer. Section 10(d)'s successor guarantee condition on page 129 remains conditional, alongside the other substitution conditions.",
    "Annual ICMA interest with no stub is selected. The reference-period and short/long-stub alternatives are not selected. Marginal branch instructions interleave raw extraction; quoted locators are not continuous operative prose.",
    "German controls and the English version is nonbinding, as selected on final terms page 7 and provided on base page 133.",
